name 'pl-aif-2-U5-promise-chain'
title 'title'
description 'description here'

markdown <<MARKDOWN
<div style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.6;">

# Tracing the Promise Timeline

<span style="font-size: 1.05em;">
In this level, we’ll trace what happens <em>over time</em> in a full Promise chain. A button click starts the request, <code style = "font-size:12pt";>fetch()</code> creates a Promise, and then <code style = "font-size:12pt";>.then()</code> / <code>.catch()</code> run later when the Promise settles.
</span>

---

## The Big Idea

<div style="text-align: center; width: 80%; margin: 0 auto;">
  <p style="
    font-size: 18px; 
    background-color: #F5F7F8; 
    padding: 10px; 
    border-left: 5px solid #8148B2; 
    border-right: 5px solid #8148B2;
    display: inline-block;
  ">
  <strong>Timeline mindset:</strong> <code style = "font-size:12pt";>fetch()</code> happens now.<br> <code style = "font-size:12pt";>.then()</code> / <code style = "font-size:12pt";>.catch()</code> happen later.
  </p>
</div>




---

## Promise Chain We’re Tracing

<div style="font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, 'Liberation Mono', 'Courier New', monospace; font-size:0.95em; background:#0b1020; color:#e5e7eb; padding:12px; border-radius:10px; overflow:auto; max-width:880px;">
button click
  → fetch(url)<br>
    .then(response =&gt; response.json())<br>
    .then(data =&gt; /* use the data */)<br>
    .catch(error =&gt; /* handle problems */)
</div>

---

## Timeline: Step-by-Step

<div style="border:1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius:14px; padding:14px; background:#ffffff; max-width:900px; margin:12px 0;">
  <div style="font-weight:800; margin-bottom:10px;">What happens in order</div>

  <!-- Timeline item 1 -->
  <div style="display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:flex-start; margin:10px 0;">
    <div style="width:28px; height:28px; border-radius:999px;  background:#5B6770; border:1px solid #e5e7eb; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-weight:800; color: #ffffff;">1</div>
    <div style="flex:1;">
      <div style="font-weight:700;">Button click starts the request</div>
      <div style="margin-top:4px; line-height:1.55;">
        Your code begins running because an event happened (the user clicked).
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-left:13px; border-left:2px dashed #e5e7eb; height:16px;"></div>

  <!-- Timeline item 2 -->
  <div style="display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:flex-start; margin:10px 0;">
    <div style="width:28px; height:28px; border-radius:999px;  background:#5B6770; border:1px solid #e5e7eb; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-weight:800; color: #ffffff;">2</div>
    <div style="flex:1;">
      <div style="font-weight:700;"><code style = "font-size:12pt">fetch()</code> creates a <span style="display:inline-block; padding:2px 8px; border-radius:999px; background:#dccbea; ">Pending</span> Promise</div>
      <div style="margin-top:4px; line-height:1.55;">
        <code style = "font-size:12pt">fetch(url)</code> returns immediately with a Promise. The request is in progress, so the Promise is <strong>pending</strong>.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-left:13px; border-left:2px dashed #e5e7eb; height:16px;"></div>

  <!-- Timeline item 3 -->
  <div style="display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:flex-start; margin:10px 0;">
    <div style="width:28px; height:28px; border-radius:999px;  background:#5B6770; border:1px solid #e5e7eb; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-weight:800; color: #ffffff;">3</div>
    <div style="flex:1;">
      <div style="font-weight:700;">You attach handlers: <code style = "font-size:12pt">.then()</code> and <code style = "font-size:12pt">.catch()</code></div>
      <div style="margin-top:4px; line-height:1.55;">
        This is you saying: “When this Promise finishes, run this code.”
        The handlers don’t run yet — they’re just <em>registered</em>.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-left:13px; border-left:2px dashed #e5e7eb; height:16px;"></div>

  <!-- Timeline item 4 -->
  <div style="display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:flex-start; margin:10px 0;">
    <div style="width:28px; height:28px; border-radius:999px;  background:#5B6770; border:1px solid #e5e7eb; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-weight:800; color: #ffffff;">4</div>
    <div style="flex:1;">
      <div style="font-weight:700;">If it succeeds, the Promise is <span style="display:inline-block; padding:2px 8px; border-radius:999px; background:#b2dee3; ">Fulfilled</span></div>
      <div style="margin-top:4px; line-height:1.55;">
        The <strong>first</strong> <code style = "font-size:12pt">.then()</code> runs with a <strong>Response</strong> object.
        Usually you convert it into usable data:
        <br/>
        <span style="font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, 'Liberation Mono', 'Courier New', monospace;">
          <code style = "font-size:12pt">.then(response =&gt; response.json())</code>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top:6px; padding:8px 10px; background:#f9fafb; border:1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius:10px; line-height:1.55;">
        <strong>Why a 2nd <code style = "font-size:12pt">.then()</code>?</strong><br/>
        <code style = "font-size:12pt">response.json()</code> is also asynchronous — it returns a Promise too.  
        The <strong>second</strong> <code style = "font-size:12pt">.then()</code> runs when that data is ready.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-left:13px; border-left:2px dashed #e5e7eb; height:16px;"></div>

  <!-- Timeline item 5 -->
  <div style="display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:flex-start; margin:10px 0;">
    <div style="width:28px; height:28px; border-radius:999px;  background:#5B6770; border:1px solid #e5e7eb; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-weight:800; color: #ffffff;">5</div>
    <div style="flex:1;">
      <div style="font-weight:700;">If anything fails, <code style = "font-size:12pt">.catch()</code> runs</div>
      <div style="margin-top:4px; line-height:1.55;">
        If the request fails (or something throws an error in the chain), the Promise becomes
        <span style="display:inline-block; padding:2px 8px; border-radius:999px; background:#f7bfbf;"><strong>Rejected</strong></span>,
        and <code style = "font-size:12pt">.catch(error =&gt; ...)</code> handles it.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

---

## What Each Part “Receives”

<div style="border:1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius:12px; padding:12px; background:#ffffff; max-width:900px; margin:12px 0;">
  <table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; font-size:0.98em;">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="text-align:left; padding:10px; border-bottom:1px solid #e5e7eb;">Part</th>
        <th style="text-align:left; padding:10px; border-bottom:1px solid #e5e7eb;">What it gets</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td style="padding:10px; border-bottom:1px solid #f0f2f5;"><code style = "font-size:12pt">fetch(url)</code></td>
        <td style="padding:10px; border-bottom:1px solid #f0f2f5; font-size: 14pt;">A <strong>Promise</strong> (starts Pending)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td style="padding:10px; border-bottom:1px solid #f0f2f5;"><code style = "font-size:12pt">.then(response =&gt; ...)</code></td>
        <td style="padding:10px; border-bottom:1px solid #f0f2f5; font-size: 14pt;">A <strong>Response</strong> (if fetch succeeded)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td style="padding:10px; border-bottom:1px solid #f0f2f5;"><code style = "font-size:12pt">.then(data =&gt; ...)</code></td>
        <td style="padding:10px; border-bottom:1px solid #f0f2f5; font-size: 14pt;">The parsed <strong>data</strong> (often JSON)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td style="padding:10px;"><code style = "font-size:12pt">.catch(error =&gt; ...)</code></td>
        <td style="padding:10px;font-size: 14pt;">An <strong>Error</strong> (if something failed)</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

---

## Mini Checkpoint


#### Try putting the steps in order. Check your answer before moving on. 

  <div style="padding-top:10px; line-height:1.6;">
    Put these in timeline order:
    <ol>
      <li style = "font-size:14pt">The <strong>second</strong> <code>.then()</code> runs with data</li>
      <li style = "font-size:14pt"><code style = "font-size:12pt">fetch()</code> returns a pending Promise</li>
      <li style = "font-size:14pt">Button click starts the request</li>
      <li style = "font-size:14pt"><code style = "font-size:12pt">.catch()</code> runs if there’s an error</li>
      <li style = "font-size:14pt">The <strong>first</strong> <code>.then()</code> runs with a Response</li>
    </ol>
  </div>


<details style="margin:10px 0; border-radius:10px; padding:10px; background:#f7f8fa; max-width:900px;">
  <summary style="cursor:pointer; font-weight:900;">Show Answer ✅</summary>
  <div style="padding-top:10px; line-height:1.6;">
    <strong>Correct order:</strong> 3 → 2 → 5 → 1 → 4<br/>
    (Button click → fetch returns Promise → first then gets Response → second then gets data → catch runs if error)
  </div>
</details>


</div>

## Next up
